  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RESTORING DESERTED AGRICULTURAL LAND FOR MIGRATORY BIRDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project acquired, with match funds, fee title for 119 wetland acres in a corridor that connects existing protected areas. On this tract, the project will: 1) remove and control invasive plants from all 119 acres; 2) remove debris and trash from drainage channels and on 30 acres along the perimeter of the property; 3) reforest 10 acres with native woody wetland species; 4) establish quarterly bird monitoring; and 5) educate 100 students and community members. The control of invasives and maintenance of the reforested area will continue for five years from the beginning of the project period. A maximum of $10,000 in NMBCA funds is approved for bird monitoring activities, which will result in an analysis of the sites and recommend management actions. Important: Restoration activities may not begin until consultation with the State Historic Preservation Office (SHPO) in Puerto Rico is complete and any SHPO requirements are met.</narrative>
  </description>
